<title>TURKEY: TURK AKCANSA Q1 LOSS TURNS TO PROFIT.</title>
<headline>TURK AKCANSA Q1 LOSS TURNS TO PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)    64.42 vs	 9.50 loss</p>
<p>    Net profit		    245.14 vs	19.27 loss</p>
<p>    Net sales		   5,026.79 vs   2,113.76</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    671.96 vs	96.28</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  131.72 vs     456.99</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 205.41 vs     572.73</p>
<p>    Total debts		 7,192.02 vs   7,166.58</p>
<p>    Equity		     15,540.25 vs   8,107.42</p>
<p>    Capital		     3,805.16 vs   2,027.38</p>
<p>NOTE - Akcansa Cimento Sanayi ve Ticaret A.S. is Turkey's biggest cement producer equally owned by Turkish Sabanci conglomerate and Belgian Cimenteries CBR SA, a unit of German Heidelberger Zement. Each partner holds a 39.72 percent stake.</p>
<p>The company began paying out a 400 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from 1996 profits from April 30.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
